=== TITLE: USG Abdomen & Pelvis (Female - Postmenopausal) ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
NORMAL POSTMENOPAUSAL USG ABDOMEN & PELVIS STUDY.
- Age-related physiological postmenopausal changes in uterus and ovaries.
- No abdominal or pelvic mass lesion.

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: ULTRASONOGRAPHY OF WHOLE ABDOMEN & PELVIS (POSTMENOPAUSAL FEMALE)

FINDINGS:
- LIVER: Normal in size and parenchymal echotexture. No focal solid or cystic mass lesion.
- GALL BLADDER: Well-distended, lumen is clear without calculus or wall thickening. CBD normal.
- PANCREAS & SPLEEN: Normal in size and morphology.
- KIDNEYS: Bilateral kidneys show normal parenchymal thickness and echotexture. No calculus or hydronephrosis.
- URINARY BLADDER: Distended with normal wall thickness. No intraluminal mass or calculus.
- UTERUS: Shows physiological postmenopausal involution, measuring 5.8 x 2.8 x 2.4 cm. Myometrium is homogeneous. Endometrial strip is thin and regular (ET: 3.2 mm).
- OVARIES: Bilateral ovaries are atrophic, consistent with postmenopausal status. No adnexal cyst or mass.
- PERITONEAL CAVITY: No free fluid, ascites, or lymphadenopathy.